\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Where the loss sits.}{7}{section*.38}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces What HAN does with the paths: each point is a path, at the search's mean preference for it (both set sizes) and HAN's mean weight for it over the sets that hold it (seed 1). The two agree on paths through users. They disagree on the near-empty category paths, which the search ranks high and HAN mostly drops (\val  {kind-empty-dropped} of \val  {kind-empty-uses} uses get a weight below \val  {weight-drop}). They also disagree on the dense category paths, which the search ranks low and HAN uses.}}{7}{figure.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:weights}{{3}{7}{What HAN does with the paths: each point is a path, at the search's mean preference for it (both set sizes) and HAN's mean weight for it over the sets that hold it (seed 1). The two agree on paths through users. They disagree on the near-empty category paths, which the search ranks high and HAN mostly drops (\val {kind-empty-dropped} of \val {kind-empty-uses} uses get a weight below \val {weight-drop}). They also disagree on the dense category paths, which the search ranks low and HAN uses}{figure.caption.37}{}}
